# SwarmGuard AI — Frontend Environment Configuration Example
#
# You usually need none of this. Leave both unset and the app talks to its own
# origin: src/config.ts defaults API_BASE_URL to "/api" and derives the
# WebSocket origin from window.location, which is exactly what nginx.conf
# proxies. That works unchanged on localhost, a LAN address and a TLS domain.
#
# The previous contents of this file were:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
#   VITE_WS_BASE_URL=ws://localhost:8000
#
# Copying those into a real deployment breaks it twice over. nginx.conf sets
# `connect-src 'self'` in its Content-Security-Policy, so the browser refuses a
# cross-origin fetch to :8000 outright; and the hostname is wrong for anything
# that is not the developer's own machine.
#
# Set these ONLY for a split deployment, where the API is served from a
# genuinely different origin than the frontend -- and then widen connect-src in
# nginx.conf to match, or the CSP will block it.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
# VITE_WS_BASE_URL=wss://api.example.com
